1
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,130
I'm ready.

2
00:00:07,290 --> 00:00:08,630
You sure?

3
00:00:07,290 --> 00:00:08,630
Uh-huh.

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,460
Okay, let me just straighten out your helmet there.

5
00:00:11,670 --> 00:00:15,340
Thanks, Daddy.

6
00:00:11,670 --> 00:00:15,340
No, no. One daddy, two mommies.

7
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:20,060
All right, it's all yours.

8
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:20,060
Okay, okay.

9
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:21,520
There you go, there you go.

10
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:26,230
Wow, Ben's first big kid's bike. This is so exciting.

11
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:28,400
Oh, yeah, I remember mine.

12
00:00:28,610 --> 00:00:31,110
It was my sixth birthday. My dad took me to the park...

13
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:34,780
...and I got on it and... it bent.  Yeah.

14
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:38,450
I never had a bike of my own.

15
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:38,450
What?

16
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:40,450
Well, we didn't have a lot of money.

17
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:43,410
But the girl across the street had the best bike.

18
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:48,040
It was pink and it had rainbow-colored tassels hanging off the handle grips...

19
00:00:48,290 --> 00:00:51,250
...and a bell, and this big, white wicker basket...

20
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:54,510
...with those plastic daisies stuck on.

21
00:00:55,050 --> 00:00:57,300
That sounds like my first bike.

22
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:00,550
My dad gave me his old one.

23
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,890
Did the girl ever let you ride it?

24
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,890
No.

25
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:06,480
But she gave me the box that it came in.

26
00:01:06,980 --> 00:01:09,810
It had a picture of the bike on the front.

27
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:14,610
So I would sit on it and my stepdad would drag me around the backyard.

28
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:17,030
That is so unfair.

29
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:20,240
Not really, I got to drag him around too.

30
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:07,040
Hey, what are you guys doing?

31
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:09,330
Making holiday candy for the neighbors.

32
00:02:09,790 --> 00:02:10,830
I'm sorry, who?

33
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:14,460
I'm gonna hang this basket on the door.

34
00:02:14,670 --> 00:02:17,630
When the neighbors walk by, they can all take a piece.

35
00:02:19,050 --> 00:02:21,260
But we don't know the neighbors.

36
00:02:19,050 --> 00:02:21,260
I do.

37
00:02:21,470 --> 00:02:24,640
There's, uh, let's see, the guy with the mustache...

38
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:28,180
...smokes-a-lot lady, some kids I've seen...

39
00:02:28,430 --> 00:02:32,440
...and the red-haired guy who does not like to be called Rusty.

40
00:02:33,110 --> 00:02:35,650
See, this is exactly why I'm making this candy.

41
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:37,990
We can learn their names and get to know our neighbors.

42
00:02:38,190 --> 00:02:40,570
Wouldn't it be easier if we just moved?

43
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:45,410
Good morning.

44
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:48,950
Ah, somebody's in a good mood.

45
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:48,950
Well, why shouldn't I be?

46
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:52,170
I have great friends. I have a wonderful job...

47
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:54,130
Where you can make out with your assistant.

48
00:02:55,630 --> 00:02:56,800
Come on, it's not a big deal.

49
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:58,840
We stayed up all night coming up with a plan...

50
00:02:59,010 --> 00:03:01,050
...so that us dating will not be a problem.

51
00:03:01,260 --> 00:03:03,050
Oh, yeah? What's the plan?

52
00:03:06,470 --> 00:03:09,730
We... We are not...

53
00:03:10,730 --> 00:03:12,640
...going to let it...

54
00:03:12,850 --> 00:03:14,520
...be a problem.

55
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:18,650
Wow. It took you all night to come up with that plan?

56
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:20,690
Oh, well, you know, we did other stuff too.

57
00:03:22,570 --> 00:03:23,660
Did you two?

58
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:26,450
Oh, Monica, you know I don't sleep with guys on the first date.

59
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:29,290
Matt Wire, Mark Lynn, Ben Wise...

60
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:29,290
Anymore.

61
00:03:36,250 --> 00:03:39,630
Hi, Tag, um, I have a conference call today, is that correct?

62
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:42,880
Yes, at 4.

63
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:42,880
Okay, thank you, that'll be all.

64
00:03:43,590 --> 00:03:44,640
Wait, wait.

65
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:50,220
Did you see that?

66
00:03:50,430 --> 00:03:53,560
That mail guy had no idea there was something going on between us.

67
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:04,740
I'd better get back to my desk.

68
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:04,740
Okay, hard worker.

69
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:08,740
I'll remember to put that in your evaluation.

70
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:12,040
My what?

71
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:12,040
You've been here for two months now...

72
00:04:12,250 --> 00:04:15,920
...and your boss is required to hand in a performance evaluation.

73
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:20,000
But you know, there is one thing that I have yet to evaluate.

74
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:30,850
Are you serious?

75
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:30,850
No, I've just always wanted to do that.

76
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:33,350
Can you help me clean this up?

77
00:04:39,190 --> 00:04:42,280
The basket is totally empty. My God, the neighbors ate all the candy.

78
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:44,070
Well, either that or, uh...

79
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:47,740
Joey.

80
00:04:49,950 --> 00:04:50,990
Yeah?

81
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:54,330
Did you eat all the neighbor candy?

82
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:54,330
Uh, well, yeah, that was the plan.

83
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:57,790
But by the time I got to it there was only a couple pieces left.

84
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,130
Yeah. They've been coming by all day. They love it.

85
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,960
They love my candy?

86
00:05:03,210 --> 00:05:06,220
Oh, man, I gotta go make more.

87
00:05:03,210 --> 00:05:06,220
Hey, Mon.

88
00:05:06,430 --> 00:05:11,390
Make some more lasagna too. Something might have happened to a huge chunk of it.

89
00:05:12,310 --> 00:05:14,470
Ross, the neighbors ate all my candy.

90
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:16,270
Mine stole my newspaper.

91
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:18,060
It's like a crime wave.

92
00:05:22,230 --> 00:05:24,400
Pheebs, you, uh, got a second?

93
00:05:24,610 --> 00:05:26,400
Sure.

94
00:05:24,610 --> 00:05:26,400
Yeah.

95
00:05:26,570 --> 00:05:29,030
Ever since you, uh, told me that story about that bike...

96
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:31,450
...I couldn't stop thinking about it.

97
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:35,370
I mean, everyone should have a first bike, you know? So...

98
00:05:39,210 --> 00:05:42,040
Oh, my God, Ross.

99
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:44,170
You like it?

100
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:44,170
I love it.

101
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:46,670
Yeah?

102
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:46,670
Oh. Oh, God...

103
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:49,180
And I love you.

104
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:49,180
Ah.

105
00:05:49,340 --> 00:05:50,800
Not that way.

106
00:05:51,470 --> 00:05:53,640
But the bike got you a lot closer.

107
00:05:51,470 --> 00:05:53,640
Oh.

108
00:05:54,310 --> 00:05:56,100
Well, uh, take it downstairs.

109
00:05:56,310 --> 00:05:58,140
You know, give it a test drive.

110
00:05:58,350 --> 00:06:00,520
Okay. Oh, my God.

111
00:06:00,980 --> 00:06:02,900
My first bike.

112
00:06:03,190 --> 00:06:06,190
Thank you for the best present I've ever gotten.

113
00:06:06,820 --> 00:06:08,320
You're welcome.

114
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:12,780
Oh, and Chandler's about to cry.

115
00:06:14,990 --> 00:06:16,240
Am not.

116
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:22,040
Who is that?

117
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:26,920
Don't worry, I'm brave. I am brave. I... I am brave.

118
00:06:28,470 --> 00:06:30,260
No, no, no, no, no.

119
00:06:31,550 --> 00:06:33,800
Can you tell me who is there, please?

120
00:06:34,890 --> 00:06:37,560
My name's Gary. I live upstairs.

121
00:06:39,890 --> 00:06:41,190
Hi.

122
00:06:39,890 --> 00:06:41,190
Hi.

123
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:43,900
Do you know what time it is?

124
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:43,900
It's candy time.

125
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:48,570
My roommate says that they taste like little drops of heaven.

126
00:06:48,780 --> 00:06:50,650
Oh, please. Heh.

127
00:06:50,990 --> 00:06:53,820
Did you hear that? "Little drops of heaven."

128
00:06:55,410 --> 00:06:56,950
Four a.m.

129
00:06:57,200 --> 00:06:59,370
So can I get some candy?

130
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:03,830
I am sorry, but some of us have to get up early and go to work.

131
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:07,590
He does not know that I am not "some of us."

132
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:12,720
Um, listen, I'm sorry, but I'll put some out first thing in the morning.

133
00:07:12,930 --> 00:07:15,300
Well, okay, I'll swing by later.

134
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,390
You live in this building?

135
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,390
Mm-hm.

136
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:20,480
Mm. Seems like I would have remembered you.

137
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:25,520
Mm. Night, Gar.

138
00:07:37,910 --> 00:07:40,250
So did you read your evaluation yet?

139
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,830
No, it was marked "confidential."

140
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:45,080
I just sent it down to human resources.

141
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:52,380
Okay, please, you're kidding, right? I wrote that one as a joke for you.

142
00:07:52,590 --> 00:07:54,430
A joke they would appreciate?

143
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:57,010
I'm thinking no.

144
00:07:57,680 --> 00:08:02,060
What did you say?

145
00:07:57,680 --> 00:08:02,060
Um, I said that you were a good kisser...

146
00:08:02,270 --> 00:08:06,610
...and, uh, that I liked your teeny, tiny tushy.

147
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:09,770
No, not my tushy.

148
00:08:09,980 --> 00:08:11,110
Well, it gets worse.

149
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:13,240
When asked if you take initiative, I wrote:

150
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:16,990
"Yes, he was able to unhook my bra with minimal supervision."

151
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:22,870
And under problems with performance, I wrote, "Dear God, I hope not."

152
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:27,540
And then, uh... And then I drew a little smiley face.

153
00:08:27,750 --> 00:08:30,960
And then a small pornographic sketch.

154
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:43,180
Ross, that is so sweet of you to get Phoebe that bike.

155
00:08:43,390 --> 00:08:45,690
When I heard the story, I almost cried.

156
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:47,400
Almost cried, huh?

157
00:08:47,650 --> 00:08:49,980
Hear that, Chandler? "Almost" cried.

158
00:08:51,230 --> 00:08:54,490
Hey, you cry every time somebody talks about Titanic.

159
00:08:54,860 --> 00:08:57,280
Those two had only each other.

160
00:08:58,450 --> 00:08:59,870
Phoebe really likes the bike, huh?

161
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:02,660
Oh, yeah. I saw her walking it down the street the other day.

162
00:09:02,870 --> 00:09:05,960
She had these flowers in the basket. It was so cute.

163
00:09:06,210 --> 00:09:08,960
Yeah, I saw her this morning walking it by the park.

164
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:13,760
Wait a minute, she was walking the bike? Both times?

165
00:09:15,010 --> 00:09:17,220
Hey, Pheebs.

166
00:09:15,010 --> 00:09:17,220
Oh, hi.

167
00:09:17,470 --> 00:09:21,260
Hey, so you enjoying the bike?

168
00:09:17,470 --> 00:09:21,260
Oh, uh-huh, so much. Heh.

169
00:09:21,970 --> 00:09:27,060
Pheebs, you, uh... You do know how to ride a bike, don't you? Heh.

170
00:09:28,850 --> 00:09:30,270
Of course.

171
00:09:32,150 --> 00:09:33,610
Can we see you ride it?

172
00:09:33,940 --> 00:09:35,440
Okay.

173
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:51,380
See?

174
00:09:59,550 --> 00:10:02,350
This is why I told you never get involved with your assistant.

175
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:05,930
And there's no such thing as keeping secrets when it comes to having affairs.

176
00:10:06,850 --> 00:10:08,940
Did you hear that, Chandler?

177
00:10:09,730 --> 00:10:11,100
No such thing.

178
00:10:12,770 --> 00:10:15,480
What happened? I'm just eating candy.

179
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:21,110
Maybe it's not as bad as I think. Maybe they didn't take it the way I meant it.

180
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:25,040
Absolutely, you know? Because "tushy" can mean both ass...

181
00:10:25,290 --> 00:10:26,790
...and good worker.

182
00:10:28,620 --> 00:10:30,710
Ugh, I just gotta get the thing back.

183
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:32,880
Rach? That sketch you mentioned?

184
00:10:33,090 --> 00:10:35,710
Might it have looked a little something like this?

185
00:10:36,130 --> 00:10:37,880
Oh, my God, Joey.

186
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:42,090
What is the matter with you?

187
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:42,090
God.

188
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:47,060
I tell you, this little talent came in handy before I could afford porn.

189
00:10:52,940 --> 00:10:57,320
Hi, I'm sorry. I know it's after hours, but I really need candy.

190
00:10:57,780 --> 00:11:00,820
I'm sorry, I can't help you. See? Rules are rules.

191
00:11:01,030 --> 00:11:04,030
Please, I have people coming from out of town today.

192
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:07,120
I told them all about your candy.

193
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:07,120
You're kidding.

194
00:11:07,330 --> 00:11:10,370
Out-of-towners, huh? Heh. What did you tell them?

195
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:14,000
I told them your candy was absolutely indescribable.

196
00:11:14,250 --> 00:11:19,210
Well, some people have been saying it's "little drops of heaven," but whatever.

197
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:23,760
Please, can't you help me out?

198
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:23,760
Hey, Chandler, do we know that lady?

199
00:11:23,970 --> 00:11:28,010
Maybe. Isn't she the woman who lives below you and has sex really loud?

200
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:30,430
All right, I'll do it just this once.

201
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:33,900
But you can't tell anybody.

202
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:33,900
Yes, yes, please, just give it to me.

203
00:11:34,150 --> 00:11:36,310
Yeah, that's her.

204
00:11:37,150 --> 00:11:39,150
Thank you.

205
00:11:37,150 --> 00:11:39,150
Unbelievable.

206
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:41,780
I can't believe that sign didn't work.

207
00:11:41,990 --> 00:11:44,990
You know what would work? Stop making candy.

208
00:11:45,910 --> 00:11:47,240
But they like it.

209
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:49,490
You mean they like you.

210
00:11:50,790 --> 00:11:51,830
Maybe.

211
00:11:52,210 --> 00:11:55,460
Is that why you became a chef, so that people would like you?

212
00:11:55,670 --> 00:11:59,750
Heh. You want to talk about getting people to like you, huh, funny man?

213
00:12:09,430 --> 00:12:12,680
Okay, now, just remember everything I taught you and you'll be fine.

214
00:12:12,890 --> 00:12:14,640
Okay? Here we go.

215
00:12:14,850 --> 00:12:16,770
Ready, set...

216
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:19,900
Wait, this seat is really uncomfortable.

217
00:12:20,150 --> 00:12:23,280
Maybe before we start we should just get another one.

218
00:12:23,490 --> 00:12:26,910
Perhaps like an airplane seat, or a beanbag chair.

219
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:32,000
Phoebe, you can't get out of this, okay? You have to learn how to ride a bike.

220
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:35,120
Why? Why do I have to learn?

221
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:40,500
Well, in case of an emergency.

222
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:40,500
What kind of emergency?

223
00:12:40,710 --> 00:12:45,180
Well, what if a man comes along and puts a gun to your head and says:

224
00:12:45,380 --> 00:12:48,050
"You ride this bike or I'll...

225
00:12:48,350 --> 00:12:50,760
I'll shoot you."

226
00:12:51,180 --> 00:12:53,520
Okay. I would ring the bell to distract him...

227
00:12:53,730 --> 00:12:57,400
...and then I would knock the gun out of his hand with a Chinese throwing star.

228
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:01,820
Okay, Phoebe, just get on the bike...

229
00:13:02,070 --> 00:13:05,860
...and, hey, I'll hold you up and push you. Okay?

230
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:08,740
You won't let go?

231
00:13:08,950 --> 00:13:10,240
No.

232
00:13:08,950 --> 00:13:10,240
You swear?

233
00:13:10,450 --> 00:13:11,700
I swear.

234
00:13:13,540 --> 00:13:15,370
Okay.

235
00:13:13,540 --> 00:13:15,370
Come on.

236
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:21,210
Here we go. All right? All right?

237
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:21,210
All right.

238
00:13:21,420 --> 00:13:23,420
Feel good? All right, try pedaling.

239
00:13:23,630 --> 00:13:26,800
That's it, you're doing great. Yes, take control.

240
00:13:27,010 --> 00:13:29,300
Yes, yes, yes.

241
00:13:27,010 --> 00:13:29,300
Whee! Hey!

242
00:13:30,470 --> 00:13:31,510
Oh, oh!

243
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:33,520
Oh, no.

244
00:13:35,270 --> 00:13:36,560
You swore.

245
00:13:36,770 --> 00:13:41,440
I just thought you were doing so well.

246
00:13:36,770 --> 00:13:41,440
I am shocked. Shocked.

247
00:13:46,030 --> 00:13:48,530
It's a legitimate learning technique.

248
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:51,030
Wow.

249
00:13:58,330 --> 00:13:59,370
Hey.

250
00:13:59,580 --> 00:14:03,960
There's, uh, some people outside asking about candy.

251
00:14:04,170 --> 00:14:07,510
They're just gonna have to wait, aren't they? I only got two hands.

252
00:14:07,970 --> 00:14:11,050
Need some help?

253
00:14:07,970 --> 00:14:11,050
No, you don't know the system.

254
00:14:11,260 --> 00:14:13,760
I don't need nobody messing with the system.

255
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:18,690
By the way, the week before your wedding, you may not see a lot of me.

256
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:31,030
Oh, hello, liar.

257
00:14:33,660 --> 00:14:37,500
Look, I'm really sorry I let go of the bike.

258
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:39,750
I could've been killed, I hope you know.

259
00:14:41,710 --> 00:14:43,500
I know, I know.

260
00:14:45,250 --> 00:14:47,380
But can we please try it again?

261
00:14:47,630 --> 00:14:49,970
I mean, you were so close, Phoebe.

262
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:52,760
Well, I would love to...

263
00:14:53,510 --> 00:14:56,760
...but the bike got stolen and the police have no suspects.

264
00:15:03,190 --> 00:15:04,480
Phoebe.

265
00:15:03,190 --> 00:15:04,480
What?

266
00:15:07,570 --> 00:15:09,440
What the hell?

267
00:15:10,950 --> 00:15:11,990
All right, you know what?

268
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:15,330
If you are not going to learn how to ride this bike, then I'm sorry...

269
00:15:15,530 --> 00:15:17,700
...I'm just gonna have to take it back.

270
00:15:15,530 --> 00:15:17,700
What? Why?

271
00:15:17,870 --> 00:15:21,120
Because. Because it's...

272
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:25,420
It'd be like you having this guitar...

273
00:15:25,630 --> 00:15:27,420
...and never playing it.

274
00:15:27,670 --> 00:15:30,550
Okay, this guitar wants to be played.

275
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:33,890
And this bike wants to be ridden.

276
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:36,390
And if you don't ride it...

277
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:40,680
...you're killing its spirit.

278
00:15:42,690 --> 00:15:43,980
The bike...

279
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:46,560
...is dying.

280
00:15:50,610 --> 00:15:55,110
All right. If you care enough to make up that load of crap, okay.

281
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:56,990
Great.

282
00:15:59,580 --> 00:16:01,620
You're making the bike very happy.

283
00:16:01,830 --> 00:16:03,080
Okay, Ross.

284
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,840
Please don't die.

285
00:16:11,420 --> 00:16:14,010
Okay, I think we can get the evaluation back before they see it.

286
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:18,680
We have to get into Mr. Zelner's office. He doesn't get in until 10, so no problem.

287
00:16:18,890 --> 00:16:22,930
But his assistant, Betty, comes in early to eat her breakfast at her desk.

288
00:16:23,140 --> 00:16:26,400
That's kind of sad.

289
00:16:23,140 --> 00:16:26,400
Yeah, well, Betty's kind of sad.

290
00:16:26,810 --> 00:16:30,570
Which is why I believe I can lure her away with these chocolates.

291
00:16:32,110 --> 00:16:34,200
Now, while I distract her, you go in the office.

292
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:35,780
Got it.

293
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:35,780
Let's roll.

294
00:16:37,490 --> 00:16:39,700
Hello, Rachel. You, uh, got a minute?

295
00:16:39,910 --> 00:16:43,250
Yeah, sure, Mr. Zelner. For you? Anything. Minute.

296
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:45,290
Okay, great.

297
00:16:45,540 --> 00:16:47,130
Abort the plan. Abort the plan.

298
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:50,590
Uh, actually, I'd like to speak to both of you.

299
00:16:51,050 --> 00:16:52,260
Okay.

300
00:16:53,010 --> 00:16:57,840
Uh, well, can we get you anything, Mr. Zelner? Maybe some chocolates?

301
00:16:58,510 --> 00:17:02,140
Um, no, thanks, but I'll give these to Betty.

302
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:06,850
So I read your evaluation of Tag.

303
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:10,440
Or, uh, to use his full name, Tag "Sweet Cheeks" Jones?

304
00:17:12,190 --> 00:17:14,360
Is something going on with you two?

305
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:19,990
Oh, my God, can you imagine if there was?

306
00:17:21,740 --> 00:17:25,330
I mean, what would happen exactly?

307
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:29,000
Well, I'd be forced to file a report.

308
00:17:29,210 --> 00:17:31,920
I'd have to consult with the legal department.

309
00:17:32,130 --> 00:17:34,670
And your future at the company would be in jeopardy.

310
00:17:36,550 --> 00:17:38,130
Well...

311
00:17:36,550 --> 00:17:38,130
Uh, Mr. Zelner...

312
00:17:38,840 --> 00:17:41,100
...I'm the one who filled in that evaluation.

313
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:42,560
Oh, no...

314
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:42,560
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

315
00:17:42,810 --> 00:17:44,810
I thought it would be funny.

316
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:48,980
You wrote that you have a cute tushy?

317
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:51,560
Yes.

318
00:17:51,770 --> 00:17:54,230
I have a weird sense of humor.

319
00:17:54,490 --> 00:17:56,990
And I'm kind of strangely proud of my butt.

320
00:17:58,450 --> 00:18:00,660
It's kind of a risky joke, Tag.

321
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:03,990
And what is this drawing? I can't figure out what this is.

322
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:07,540
You're looking at it upside down... You know what? It doesn't matter.

323
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:11,460
Hey, it's not like I don't have a sense of humor, huh?

324
00:18:11,670 --> 00:18:15,250
Hell, I even enjoy a naughty limerick every now and then.

325
00:18:17,880 --> 00:18:19,510
But there's a time and a place, huh?

326
00:18:21,510 --> 00:18:24,220
Unless you, uh, have a limerick right now.

327
00:18:26,810 --> 00:18:30,560
No? Okay. Well, uh, you've got my fax number.

328
00:18:38,610 --> 00:18:41,200
I can't believe you did that. That was really sweet.

329
00:18:41,410 --> 00:18:44,280
Ah, don't worry about it.

330
00:18:41,410 --> 00:18:44,280
No, you could've lost your job.

331
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:47,750
Are you kidding me? With a cute butt like this, I'd find work.

332
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:51,920
Thank you, you're great.

333
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:55,920
You know what?

334
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:55,920
What?

335
00:18:56,210 --> 00:18:58,010
I feel great.

336
00:18:58,630 --> 00:19:00,510
In fact...

337
00:19:05,220 --> 00:19:06,260
What?

338
00:19:06,970 --> 00:19:10,850
It's just... It took me so long to get that desk organized.

339
00:19:11,230 --> 00:19:13,020
I'm sorry.

340
00:19:14,150 --> 00:19:16,070
There it is.

341
00:19:27,950 --> 00:19:29,160
What is going on?

342
00:19:29,370 --> 00:19:32,750
We're waiting for the candy. Bring out the candy.

343
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:35,330
Yeah, lady, give us candy.

344
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:37,920
Joey.

345
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:41,010
What's up, buddy?

346
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:41,010
What are you doing?

347
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:44,300
Waiting to get candy.

348
00:19:44,930 --> 00:19:46,600
Get in here.

349
00:19:46,890 --> 00:19:50,350
Hey, and you cannot smoke in here.

350
00:19:53,850 --> 00:19:55,230
Merry Christmas.

351
00:19:56,440 --> 00:20:00,650
Okay, guys, the candy is coming. I just need 15 minutes for the chocolate to cool.

352
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:06,820
All right, everybody, just be quiet. Be quiet. Be quiet. Pipe down.

353
00:20:07,030 --> 00:20:09,160
What is the matter with you people?

354
00:20:09,370 --> 00:20:12,500
This woman was trying to do a nice thing for you.

355
00:20:12,710 --> 00:20:16,170
She was making candy so she could try to get to know all of you...

356
00:20:16,380 --> 00:20:19,840
...and I'll bet that not one of you can tell me her name.

357
00:20:20,050 --> 00:20:21,510
Am I right?

358
00:20:22,220 --> 00:20:24,090
Candy Lady?

359
00:20:25,390 --> 00:20:27,720
No, not "Candy Lady."

360
00:20:28,470 --> 00:20:30,850
If we know it, can we have candy?

361
00:20:32,020 --> 00:20:33,770
All right, you know what?

362
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:36,520
Forget it. All of you, forget it. You've ruined it.

363
00:20:36,730 --> 00:20:38,770
Go home. You've ruined it. You've ruined it.

364
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:42,740
That's all wrong. You guys ruined everything. You ruined it.

365
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:52,120
Thank you.

366
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:52,120
You're welcome.

367
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,290
Did you smoke?

368
00:20:55,960 --> 00:21:01,380
No, smokes-a-lot lady blew smoke directly into my mouth.

369
00:21:02,380 --> 00:21:03,760
Uh, are you okay?

370
00:21:03,970 --> 00:21:06,590
I'm fine now, but it was really scary there for a while.

371
00:21:06,800 --> 00:21:09,890
Someone slipped a threatening note under the door.

372
00:21:10,100 --> 00:21:14,020
Oh, yeah. Sorry about that. Mob mentality or whatever. I don't know.

373
00:21:24,780 --> 00:21:27,910
I can't believe it. I did it. I rode a bike.

374
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:31,240
I never thought I'd be able to do that. Thank you, Ross.

375
00:21:31,450 --> 00:21:33,790
Oh, hey, don't thank me. Thank yourself.

376
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:37,830
You're the one who faced your fears and ultimately overcame them.

377
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:41,920
Don't be so corny, Ross. It's not an After School Special.

